  "acceptance_holds": [
    "Every modified body shell, rear cassette, and bottom keel must remain one closed manifold component.",
    "The seated keel must clear both lower shells and the rear cassette; the seated rear cassette must clear all four body shells.",
    "The keel must install from below before the cassette, and the cassette must install from the rear with zero sampled sweep collision.",
    "One round datum, one lateral secondary slot, and longitudinal tolerance slots must avoid pin-against-pin assembly and avoid using fasteners to pull misaligned parts into place.",
    "All eight M3 screw heads and hex-key approach envelopes must remain directly accessible from the bottom.",
    "The gasket lips are cosmetic weather-control features only and may not enter the aluminum primary load path.",
    "The central wire-channel keepout and rear exit must remain clear of all printed seam features and frozen aluminum envelopes.",
    "Two forward drains must remain open, printable, and outside the protected wire channel.",
    "Heat-set insert fit, EPDM compression, drain performance, wire-exit sealing, seam stiffness, and assembly tolerance require a physical seam coupon.",
    "The six shared rear-facing M5 structural pads and backplate attachment remain a coordinated shell/aluminum hold and are not replaced by these eight cosmetic M3 seam screws.",
    "Glow-panel, eye, ear, socket, final body-seam, and complete hardware/tool validation remain production blockers.",
